Significance: minor
Type: added

Recurring events can now be authored from the event editor. A Repeat toggle in the Event settings panel opens controls for how often an event repeats, daily, weekly, monthly or yearly, on which weekdays, on which day or which ordinal weekday of the month, and whether the series never ends, ends on a date, or ends after a set number of dates. Below it, an Occurrences list shows the dates the rule produces and lets an organizer cancel any one of them and restore it again, without disturbing the rest of the series. Recurrence needs a named timezone such as America/New_York, so on an event set to a fixed UTC offset the toggle is disabled and says so. In the admin events list a recurring series stays one row, now marked as recurring and dated from the occurrence it is next doing rather than from the date the series first ran, and sorting by event date follows the date each row shows.
